A||||3||Ed||Sears Point Historics||||1||
Z||000000||Ed||05-20-2000||12:40 AM||||Went to Sears Point Raceway north of San Francisco today.  They're having historic sports car races over this weekend.  Cars had to have been built before about 1965 or so.  Ferraris, Cobras, Porsches, Lolas, Comets!, Hudsons!, an old Chrysler! (c. 1951), and some Trans Am sedans for you heavy iron American V-8 types (Challengers, AMX's, Camaros, Moosetangs,) most having some racing history.  <P>Interesting to compare what is said on this board about upgrades, etc. against what is actually being road raced.  <P>||||reg||1
